family and friends are remembering the  man who died after what police are  calling a road rage incident 73-year-old  marlon smith died yesterday after being  run over by a vehicle on boulder highway  and desert inn  smith's best friend spoke to victoria  saha reflecting on a man lost too soon  to a senseless tragedy  i hope they live in the shame of this  the rest of their lives  harsh words from marlin smith's best  friend larry gandy to the person who ran  smith over on tuesday  stay in jail police say the driver of a  suburban was said to have cut smith off  smith honked a passenger in the suburban  through a beer can at smith's jeep  smith then got out of his car to  confront the occupants  and was run over gandhi says smith's  wife  saw the whole thing it's just  disheartening there's  there's no punishment grave enough for  these guys gandy describes smith who  also went by the name  fuzzy by his motorcycle group as a  kind-hearted person  just a sweet guy one time my motorcycle  broke down  he came over here at night and we worked  for three hours we went and bought  parts we went all over the place just he  just didn't want to leave me stranded  gandy saw smith about two weeks ago  and now all he has left are memories of  their motorcycle rides  a sadness that i can't explain to you  you know when you lose a brother  who survived vietnam and  all the hell you went through and then  to  be run over by two guys in the street  and left in the hot pavement to die  you know in front of his poor little  wife  the man smith used to ride motorcycles  with will be hosting a ride  this saturday in honor of him reporting  from boulder highway and desert inn  victoria saha  8 news now the family has set up a  gofundme to pay for funeral expenses you  can find that if you'd like to help out  over on our website
 

